  25. Veined octopuses carry coconut
      shell halves around and use them
      as portable shelters.
  26. Gloomy octopuses have been
      recorded throwing silt and shells,
      sometimes at other octopuses.
  27. In 2016, an octopus named Inky
      escaped from a New Zealand
      aquarium by slipping into a
      drainpipe that led to the sea.
  28. Octopuses edit their RNA far more
      than most animals, which may help
      them adapt to changes in
      temperature.
  29. Sleeping octopuses go through an
      active phase of twitching and
      color change that some researchers
      compare to dreaming.
  30. In 2022, the UK formally
      recognized octopuses as sentient
      beings in its animal welfare law.

